al retries; (b) the operation receipt that sessckpt already writes after a capture must be reconciled with this journal — adopt/extend sessckpt's receipt rather than introducing a parallel receipt shape, or document precisely why they are distinct records; (c) status-first recovery: a Recover(journal) evaluator that, after a simulated crash + clean restart, reads durable facts first (journal, receipts, blobs, markers, the bridge/provider transaction state) and classifies exactly one 13.13 outcome with the evidence record the gate requires (boundary ID, path, operation IDs, pre/post durable facts, external effect + status probe, winning lease before/after, native identity/binding before/after, selected outcome), failing closed to recoverable_parked_state on missing, stale, contradictory or ambiguous evidence, and executing explicit_rollback only as an allowed abort/closure that removes only inert staging or restores predecessors; (d) parked outcomes recorded durably with the retained lease, exact IDs, checkpoint/native identity and last error, never a fourth outcome; (e) no CLI, no mesh RPC, no provider plugin or bridge process — model their transaction states as inputs. Tests: drive every phase transition (legal and illegal), every token/ID rule, the byte-unequal retry refusal, each journal-observable 13.12 row, and each CR-MAT-01..08 boundary with a real crash injection (the sessckpt hook pattern or a child process killed at the seam) followed by Recover, asserting the exact outcome and evidence; negatives for every refusal; idempotency (same IDs + byte-equal body replays the recorded result without a second effect); narrowing mutants per refusal/transition with a shipped harness and an applied harmless SURVIVED control; a conformance matrix mapping each 10.6/13.12/13.13 clause to a test or a stated bound. Story-close items you must carry (from the 14yo67 review verdict): update internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json section:5.4 (and your own 10.6/13.12/13.13 bindings) to the real production declarations with honest coverage text and re-pin reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 to the reviewed projection (precedent: STORY-260830-3drr2m/3jqsx1 story commits), add the README section for internal/sessckpt (with test commands, no capability claim) beside your own package section, and add the forged-Admit same-epoch foreign-lease negative to internal/sessckpt (the CR-TASK-260830-14yo67-1 verdict §4 named it untested). Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-2rqigd whose tip is the 14yo67 checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-3k3e6m and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD: production-entry tests with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites, negatives, narrowing mutants with per-plant raw logs and subprocess exits, crash/idempotency, conformance matrix, no unsupported claims. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in. Attach TASK-260830-3k3e6m_results.md, TASK-260830-3k3e6m_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-3k3e6m_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-3k3e6m --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","final_result":true}}}
