{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":198,"recorded_at":1780531400000391,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3"},"task_id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5727 line(s) above)\n5728|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n5729|\n5730|Materialization Journal schema\n5731|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5732|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n5733|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n5734|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5735|\n5736|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5737|| --- | --- | --- |\n5738|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n5739|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n5740|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n5741|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n5742|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n5743|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n5744|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n5745|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n5746|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n5747|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n5748|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n5749|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n5750|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5751|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5752|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5753|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n5754|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n5755|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n5756|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n5757|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n5758|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n5759|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n5760|\n5761|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n5762|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5763|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n5764|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n5765|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n5766|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n5767|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n5768|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n5769|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n5770|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n5771|\n5772|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n5773|\n5774|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5775|| --- | --- | --- |\n5776|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n5777|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5778|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n5779|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n5780|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n5781|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n5782|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5783|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5784|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5785|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n5786|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n5787|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n5788|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n5789|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5790|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5791|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5792|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n5793|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n5794|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n5795|\n5796|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n5797|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n5798|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n5799|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n5800|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n5801|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n5802|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n5803|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n5804|\n5805|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n5806|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n5807|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n5808|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n5809|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n5810|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n5811|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n5812|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n5813|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n5814|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n5815|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n5816|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n5817|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n5818|\n5819|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n5820|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n5821|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n5822|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n5823|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n5824|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n5825|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n5826|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n5827|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n5828|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n5829|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n5830|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n5831|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n5832|rollback root MUST equal\n5833|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n5834|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n5835|provider backup location.\n5836|\n5837|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n5838|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n5839|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n5840|\n5841|Normative example:\n5842|\n5843|~~~json\n5844|{\n5845|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n5846|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n5847|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n5848|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5849|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n5850|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n5851|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n5852|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5853|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5854|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n5855|  \"authority_states\": {\n5856|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n5857|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5858|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n5859|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n5860|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n5861|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5862|    },\n5863|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n5864|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5865|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n5866|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n5867|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n5868|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5869|    }\n5870|  },\n5871|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n5872|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n5873|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n5874|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n5875|  },\n5876|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n5877|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n5878|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n5879|  ],\n5880|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n5881|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n5882|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n5883|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5884|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n5885|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n5886|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n5887|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5888|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5889|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5890|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n5891|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n5892|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5893|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5894|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5895|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5896|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n5897|    },\n5898|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n5899|  },\n5900|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n5901|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n5902|  \"last_error\": null,\n5903|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n5904|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5905|  \"extensions\": {}\n5906|}\n5907|~~~\n5908|\n5909|The two map members above are the normative\n5910|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n5911|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n5912|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n5913|\n5914|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n5915|| --- | --- | --- |\n5916|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n5917|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n5918|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n5919|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n5920|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n5921|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n5922|\n5923|The following embedded value is the normative\n5924|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n5925|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n5926|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n5927|\n5928|~~~json\n5929|{\n5930|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n5931|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5932|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n5933|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n5934|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n5935|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n5936|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n5937|  \"import_token\": null,\n5938|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n5939|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n5940|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n5941|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n5942|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n5943|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n5944|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n5945|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n5946|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5947|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n5948|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n5949|}\n5950|~~~\n5951|\n5952|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n5953|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n5954|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n5955|\n5956|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n5957|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n5958|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n5959|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n5960|   mutation.\n5961|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n5962|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n5963|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n5964|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n5965|   authoritative.\n5966|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n5967|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n5968|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n5969|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n5970|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n5971|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n5972|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n5973|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n5974|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n5975|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n5976|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n5977|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n5978|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n5979|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n5980|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n5981|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n5982|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n5983|\n5984|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n5985|cases are mandatory:\n5986|\n5987|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n5988|| --- | --- | --- |\n5989|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n5990|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n5991|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n5992|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n5993|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n5994|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n5995|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n5996|\n5997|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n5998|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n5999|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n6000|\n6001|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n6002|\n6003|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n6004|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n6005|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n6006|Its closed object contains exactly:\n6007|\n6008|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n6009|| --- | --- | --- |\n6010|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n6011|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n6012|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>managed_replica_marker</code> |\n6013|| <code>marker_id</code> | digest | JCS identity with this field omitted |\n6014|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable identity of one host/path replica across updates |\n6015|| <code>host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Host on which the marker is authoritative |\n6016|| <code>platform</code> | enum | <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>, <code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code> |\n6017|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Exact materialized group |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":199,"recorded_at":1780531400000393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3"},"task_id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0adcc-8957-7ba3-90c6-64ac412d4ec3"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":200,"recorded_at":1780531400000395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcc83f873e49b174a44f42ecaf9","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5727 line(s) above)\n5728|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n5729|\n5730|Materialization Journal schema\n5731|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5732|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n5733|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n5734|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5735|\n5736|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5737|| --- | --- | --- |\n5738|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n5739|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n5740|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n5741|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n5742|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n5743|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n5744|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n5745|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n5746|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n5747|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n5748|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n5749|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n5750|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5751|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5752|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5753|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n5754|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n5755|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n5756|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n5757|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n5758|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n5759|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n5760|\n5761|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n5762|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5763|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n5764|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n5765|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n5766|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n5767|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n5768|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n5769|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n5770|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n5771|\n5772|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n5773|\n5774|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5775|| --- | --- | --- |\n5776|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n5777|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5778|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n5779|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n5780|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n5781|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n5782|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5783|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5784|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5785|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n5786|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n5787|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n5788|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n5789|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5790|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5791|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5792|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n5793|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n5794|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n5795|\n5796|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n5797|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n5798|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n5799|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n5800|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n5801|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n5802|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n5803|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n5804|\n5805|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n5806|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n5807|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n5808|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n5809|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n5810|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n5811|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n5812|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n5813|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n5814|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n5815|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n5816|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n5817|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n5818|\n5819|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n5820|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n5821|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n5822|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n5823|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n5824|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n5825|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n5826|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n5827|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n5828|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n5829|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n5830|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n5831|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n5832|rollback root MUST equal\n5833|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n5834|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n5835|provider backup location.\n5836|\n5837|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n5838|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n5839|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n5840|\n5841|Normative example:\n5842|\n5843|~~~json\n5844|{\n5845|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n5846|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n5847|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n5848|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5849|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n5850|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n5851|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n5852|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5853|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5854|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n5855|  \"authority_states\": {\n5856|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n5857|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5858|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n5859|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n5860|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n5861|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5862|    },\n5863|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n5864|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5865|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n5866|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n5867|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n5868|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5869|    }\n5870|  },\n5871|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n5872|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n5873|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n5874|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n5875|  },\n5876|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n5877|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n5878|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n5879|  ],\n5880|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n5881|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n5882|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n5883|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5884|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n5885|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n5886|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n5887|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5888|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5889|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5890|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n5891|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n5892|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5893|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5894|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5895|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5896|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n5897|    },\n5898|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n5899|  },\n5900|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n5901|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n5902|  \"last_error\": null,\n5903|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n5904|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5905|  \"extensions\": {}\n5906|}\n5907|~~~\n5908|\n5909|The two map members above are the normative\n5910|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n5911|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n5912|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n5913|\n5914|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n5915|| --- | --- | --- |\n5916|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n5917|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n5918|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n5919|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n5920|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n5921|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n5922|\n5923|The following embedded value is the normative\n5924|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n5925|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n5926|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n5927|\n5928|~~~json\n5929|{\n5930|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n5931|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5932|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n5933|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n5934|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n5935|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n5936|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n5937|  \"import_token\": null,\n5938|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n5939|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n5940|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n5941|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n5942|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n5943|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n5944|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n5945|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n5946|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5947|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n5948|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n5949|}\n5950|~~~\n5951|\n5952|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n5953|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n5954|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n5955|\n5956|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n5957|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n5958|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n5959|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n5960|   mutation.\n5961|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n5962|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n5963|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n5964|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n5965|   authoritative.\n5966|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n5967|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n5968|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n5969|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n5970|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n5971|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n5972|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n5973|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n5974|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n5975|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n5976|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n5977|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n5978|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n5979|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n5980|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n5981|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n5982|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n5983|\n5984|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n5985|cases are mandatory:\n5986|\n5987|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n5988|| --- | --- | --- |\n5989|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n5990|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n5991|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n5992|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n5993|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n5994|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n5995|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n5996|\n5997|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n5998|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n5999|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n6000|\n6001|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n6002|\n6003|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n6004|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n6005|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n6006|Its closed object contains exactly:\n6007|\n6008|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n6009|| --- | --- | --- |\n6010|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n6011|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n6012|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>managed_replica_marker</code> |\n6013|| <code>marker_id</code> | digest | JCS identity with this field omitted |\n6014|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable identity of one host/path replica across updates |\n6015|| <code>host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Host on which the marker is authoritative |\n6016|| <code>platform</code> | enum | <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>, <code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code> |\n6017|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Exact materialized group |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
