{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c579","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":279,"recorded_at":1780531400000553,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcc9f47705cb62014e94e6785ab","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5282 line(s) above)\n5283|### 10.5 Materialization Plan\n5284|\n5285|Materialization Plan schema\n5286|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan</code> version <code>1.0.0</code> is\n5287|immutable and authorizes only the exact staged changes it lists. It is not an\n5288|ownership grant.\n5289|\n5290|Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5291|\n5292|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5293|| --- | --- | --- |\n5294|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Plan schema identifier |\n5295|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n5296|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n5297|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n5298|| <code>intent</code> | enum | <code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5299|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Logical session for provider/task-board/composite; Workspace Group for workspace-only |\n5300|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated immutable recovery base |\n5301|| <code>source_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[1..1024] | Complete source-checkpoint manifest/bundle inputs |\n5302|| <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Empty except for exact fork projections |\n5303|| <code>fork_projection</code> | Fork Workspace Projection or null | Non-null exactly for <code>intent = fork</code> |\n5304|| <code>prepared_for_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Only this allowlisted host may execute the plan |\n5305|| <code>source_lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero; exact source checkpoint lease |\n5306|| <code>source_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Exact source checkpoint fencing token |\n5307|| <code>authorities</code> | RootAuthority[0..512] | Empty only for the provider backend-identity validation-only variant; otherwise closed destination-local roots defined below |\n5308|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only when destination is classified absent or empty |\n5309|| <code>operations</code> | PlanOperation[0..65536] | Consecutive sequence beginning at 1 when non-empty |\n5310|| <code>exclusions</code> | sorted unique exclusion-class[0..128] | Exact capture/materialization policy classes |\n5311|| <code>validations</code> | sorted unique validation-name[1..6] | Required pre-commit checks from the closed registry below |\n5312|| <code>commit_strategy</code> | enum | <code>validation_only</code>, <code>atomic_directory_rename</code>, <code>atomic_file_merge</code>, <code>single_root_transaction</code>, or <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5313|| <code>rollback_required</code> | boolean | MUST be true in 1.0.0 |\n5314|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Plan author; normally destination host |\n5315|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n5316|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n5317|\n5318|<code>RootAuthority</code> is a closed tagged union, sorted by\n5319|<code>authority_id</code>. IDs use the Section 7.5 <code>root-id</code> grammar,\n5320|are unique in the plan, and are routing labels rather than cross-host\n5321|identities:\n5322|\n5323|| Tag | Exact members |\n5324|| --- | --- |\n5325|| <code>kind = workspace</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:workspace</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_replace&#124;managed_copy&#124;managed_worktree</code> |\n5326|| <code>kind = provider_store</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:provider_store</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_merge</code> |\n5327|| <code>kind = task_board_staging</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:task_board_staging</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>bridge_protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>staging_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:staged_install</code> |\n5328|\n5329|A workspace authority's logical root MUST exist in destination configuration,\n5330|its root path MUST equal that resolved mapping, and its group ID MUST equal the\n5331|referenced workspace manifest. A provider-store authority is valid only when\n5332|returned by the exact destination adapter's materialize plan and independently\n5333|accepted by the Section 7.5 root/exclusion checks. A task-board staging root\n5334|MUST be a fresh owner-only child of the resolved ax state root and MUST contain\n5335|no pre-existing manager state. Authorities MUST be pairwise path-disjoint;\n5336|neither a symlink nor a reparse point may make them overlap. Ax data, cache,\n5337|runtime, credential, authentication, SSH, and live manager roots are forbidden\n5338|except for the exact fresh task-board staging child.\n5339|\n5340|<code>ForkWorkspaceProjection</code> is a closed object containing exactly:\n5341|\n5342|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5343|| --- | --- | --- |\n5344|| <code>projection_version</code> | enum | Literal <code>workspace_fork_v1</code> |\n5345|| <code>source_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session whose checkpoint is the immutable source |\n5346|| <code>source_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Source group named by the checkpoint closure |\n5347|| <code>source_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact source topology record |\n5348|| <code>source_workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Exact source workspace-group Transfer Manifest |\n5349|| <code>destination_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Newly allocated fork session |\n5350|| <code>destination_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Fresh group identity |\n5351|| <code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact derived Workspace Group Record identity |\n5352|| <code>destination_display_name</code> | string[1..128] | New topology display name |\n5353|| <code>destination_created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Destination record author |\n5354|| <code>destination_created_at</code> | timestamp | Destination record creation time |\n5355|| <code>destination_extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS Workspace Group Record extensions |\n5356|| <code>member_mappings</code> | ForkMemberMapping[1..256] | Sorted by source workspace ID; one-to-one and onto destination members |\n5357|| <code>manifest_mappings</code> | ForkManifestMapping[1..1024] | Sorted by source manifest ID; complete bottom-up re-identification map |\n5358|\n5359|<code>ForkMemberMapping</code> contains exactly\n5360|<code>source_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5361|<code>destination_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5362|<code>group_relative_path:path</code>. The relative path MUST equal the path in\n5363|both topology records; every destination ID is fresh and unique. The complete\n5364|destination Workspace Group Record is constructed with the fixed schema and\n5365|version, record/subject/group IDs from these projection fields, the displayed\n5366|name/creation/extensions fields, and the source record's member objects in\n5367|source workspace-ID order after replacing only each workspace ID according to\n5368|<code>member_mappings</code>. Its recomputed record ID MUST equal\n5369|<code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> before persistence.\n5370|<code>ForkManifestMapping</code> contains exactly\n5371|<code>kind:workspace_group|workspace_tree</code>,\n5372|<code>source_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5373|<code>destination_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5374|<code>source_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5375|<code>destination_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>. Ax derives a destination manifest\n5376|by copying every non-identity field, entry, descriptor, and blob reference from\n5377|the source; replacing the subject, group, member, and child-manifest identities\n5378|according to the two maps; and recomputing child identities before parent\n5379|identities. It MUST persist the destination topology and all destination\n5380|manifests before publishing the fork Session Record. Source objects and bytes\n5381|remain unchanged. <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> MUST equal exactly the\n5382|destination IDs in <code>manifest_mappings</code> and MUST NOT occur in\n5383|<code>source_manifest_ids</code>.\n5384|\n5385|The following table is the complete major-v1 plan-kind tagged-union contract.\n5386|Anything not explicitly allowed in its row is forbidden:\n5387|\n5388|| <code>kind</code> | Subject and source inputs | Required authority/action set | Required validations | Legal commit strategies |\n5389|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n5390|| <code>workspace</code> | Subject is the destination Workspace Group. Exactly one workspace-group Transfer Manifest, plus its closed child manifests, is selected from <code>source_manifest_ids</code> or, for a fork, <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>. | One or more <code>workspace</code> authorities; only <code>install_workspace_group</code>, <code>install_workspace_tree</code>, <code>delete_managed_path</code>, or <code>replace_managed_replica</code>. At least one install operation is required. | Exactly <code>manifest_closure</code> and <code>workspace_state</code> | <code>atomic_directory_rename</code> for one directory boundary; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for one authority with file boundaries only; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5391|| <code>provider</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one provider Transfer Manifest is selected. A backend-resolved provider with <code>portable_store=false</code> uses the required zero-entry provider manifest that references its Provider Identity Record. | For a portable store, one or more <code>provider_store</code> authorities and only <code>merge_provider_store</code>. For a backend-resolved identity, no authorities and no operations. | <code>manifest_closure</code> plus exactly one of <code>provider_native_discovery</code> or <code>backend_identity</code> | <code>validation_only</code> only for the zero-operation backend path; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for file boundaries; <code>single_root_transaction</code> for one provider-store authority with any directory boundary; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5392|| <code>task_board</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one Task-board Bundle is selected. | Exactly one <code>task_board_staging</code> authority and exactly one <code>install_task_board_bundle</code> operation at <code>authority_root</code>. | <code>manifest_closure</code>, <code>task_board_bundle</code>, and <code>task_board_validate</code> exactly when the projected board kind is <code>local</code> | <code>single_root_transaction</code> |\n5393|| <code>composite</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one workspace-group manifest and exactly one provider manifest or Task-board Bundle are selected; never both provider and task-board branches. Fork-derived workspace manifests are allowed only with <code>intent=fork</code>. | The disjoint union of the corresponding workspace row and exactly one provider or task-board row. | Exact union of the component rows | <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> when both components mutate; when the provider component is <code>validation_only</code>, use the workspace row's one-root strategy because only workspace bytes mutate |\n5394|\n5395|<code>intent=fork</code> requires non-null <code>fork_projection</code> and a\n5396|non-empty <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>; every other intent requires null\n5397|and an empty array. For a fork plan, <code>subject_id</code> is the destination\n5398|session for provider, task-board, or composite kinds and is the destination\n5399|group for workspace kind. A plan MUST reject a source ID that is not in the\n5400|validated checkpoint closure, a derived ID that is not produced by the exact\n5401|projection, or an authority/action/validation/strategy combination outside its\n5402|row.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":280,"recorded_at":1780531400000555,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcca14376e6acff4cbeaafc3087","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1982 line(s) above)\n1983|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1984|\n1985|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1986|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1987|\n1988|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1989|| --- | --- | --- |\n1990|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1991|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1992|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1993|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1994|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1995|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1996|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1997|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1998|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1999|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n2000|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n2001|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n2002|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n2003|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2004|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n2005|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2006|\n2007|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n2008|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n2010|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n2011|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n2012|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n2013|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n2014|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n2015|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2016|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2017|new checkpoint.\n2018|\n2019|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2020|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2021|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2022|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2023|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2024|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2025|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2026|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2027|checkpoints are invalid.\n2028|\n2029|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2030|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2031|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2032|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2033|\n2034|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2035|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2036|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2037|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2038|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2039|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2040|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2041|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2042|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2043|\n2044|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2045|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2046|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2047|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2048|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2049|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2050|\n2051|Normative example:\n2052|\n2053|~~~json\n2054|{\n2055|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2056|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2057|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2058|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2059|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2060|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2061|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2062|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2063|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2064|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2065|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2066|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2067|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2068|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2069|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2070|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2071|  },\n2072|  \"event_heads\": [\n2073|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2074|  ],\n2075|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2076|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2077|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2078|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2079|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2080|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2081|  \"extensions\": {}\n2082|}\n2083|~~~\n2084|\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2088|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2089|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2090|\n2091|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2092|| --- | --- | --- |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":281,"recorded_at":1780531400000557,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcca398757d86002e0105759e6b","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/store.go`.\n1|package sessckpt\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"os\"\n7|\t\"path/filepath\"\n8|\t\"runtime\"\n9|\t\"sync\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// ErrInvalidCheckpoint reports a checkpoint closure that must be\n15|// refused before publication. It always wraps\n16|// canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so errors.Is proves the SPEC\n17|// Section 5.4 incompatible_schema class for every unpublishable\n18|// closure, including the CP-N1..CP-N4 fixtures.\n19|var ErrInvalidCheckpoint = errors.New(\"invalid checkpoint closure\")\n20|\n21|// ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the same\n22|// capture operation retried with moved inputs\n23|// (idempotency_mismatch), or a digest path holding bytes that\n24|// disagree with the installing candidate (a torn store, never a\n25|// second version of an immutable record).\n26|var ErrCheckpointConflict = errors.New(\"checkpoint capture conflict\")\n27|\n28|// Store durably installs Checkpoint Records and their operation\n29|// receipts under one data root. Checkpoint blobs are\n30|// content-addressed and installed no-replace, so capture is\n31|// append-only by construction and there is no update or delete\n32|// entry to test.\n33|//\n34|// BeforeWrite fires after validation and before the first durable\n35|// byte; AfterBlob fires after the checkpoint blob is durable and\n36|// before the operation receipt; AfterCommit fires after the receipt\n37|// is durable. All three are nil in normal operation. Tests connect\n38|// them to a secconftest Injector firing the owner's own points: a\n39|// fault before any durable byte carries safe_retry, a fault past\n40|// any durable step carries recoverable_parked_state until the\n41|// identical retry replays the recorded result, and a fault past\n42|// the receipt carries safe_retry through the replayed receipt.\n43|type Store struct {\n44|\troot        string\n45|\tmutex       sync.Mutex\n46|\tBeforeWrite func() error\n47|\tAfterBlob   func() error\n48|\tAfterCommit func() error\n49|}\n50|\n51|// Open binds a checkpoint store to the checkpoints namespace beneath\n52|// dataRoot, creating it owner-only when absent. The root must be\n53|// absolute.\n54|func Open(dataRoot string) (*Store, error) {\n55|\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dataRoot) {\n56|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: data root %q is not absolute\", ErrInvalidCheckpoint, dataRoot)\n57|\t}\n58|\troot := filepath.Join(dataRoot, \"checkpoints\")\n59|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o700); err != nil {\n60|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoints root %q: %w\", root, err)\n61|\t}\n62|\t// The operations namespace shares the root so one data-root\n63|\t// fsync discipline covers blobs and receipts together.\n64|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \"operations\"), 0o700); err != nil {\n65|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoint operations root: %w\", err)\n66|\t}\n67|\treturn &Store{root: root}, nil\n68|}\n69|\n70|// CheckpointRef names one durably installed Checkpoint Record: its\n71|// canonical digest and the operation receipt that installed it.\n72|type CheckpointRef struct {\n73|\tCheckpointID string\n74|\tOperationID  string\n75|}\n76|\n77|// checkpointFileName maps a validated checkpoint digest to its blob\n78|// file name. The digest passed scalar grammar before install;\n79|// invalid input maps to a sentinel name that can never collide\n80|// with a real blob.\n81|func checkpointFileName(checkpointID string) string {\n82|\tdigest, err := scalar.ParseDigest(checkpointID)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n85|\t}\n86|\treturn digest.Hex() + \".json\"\n87|}\n88|\n89|// operationFileName maps a validated operation UUID to its receipt\n90|// file name. UUIDv7 grammar keeps the file name an exact,\n91|// case-stable rendering of the operation identity.\n92|func operationFileName(operationID string) string {\n93|\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(operationID)\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n96|\t}\n97|\treturn id.String() + \".json\"\n98|}\n99|\n100|// installBlob installs one content-addressed blob idempotently\n101|// through the no-replace open first: a fresh path is created\n102|// atomically, and only an EEXIST loser falls back to comparing\n103|// against the winner's bytes — identical bytes are reused,\n104|// disagreeing bytes report the torn store for refusal. Leading\n105|// with the exclusive create (instead of stat-then-act) keeps the\n106|// no-replace property a filesystem fact under a second process,\n107|// not a check-then-act race the store mutex cannot see: the mutex\n108|// serializes one process, while O_EXCL serializes all of them.\n109|func installBlob(path string, data []byte) error {\n110|\tif err := writeExclusive(path, data); err == nil {\n111|\t\treturn syncDirectory(filepath.Dir(path))\n112|\t} else if !os.IsExist(err) {\n113|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"install checkpoint blob: %w\", err)\n114|\t}\n115|\texisting, readErr := os.ReadFile(path)\n116|\tif readErr != nil {\n117|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"read checkpoint blob for compare: %w\", readErr)\n118|\t}\n119|\tif string(existing) != string(data) {\n120|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: digest path holds disagreeing bytes\", ErrCheckpointConflict)\n121|\t}\n122|\treturn nil\n123|}\n124|\n125|// writeExclusive installs bytes at a path that must not exist. The\n126|// no-replace open makes append-only a filesystem property, not a\n127|// convention. Bytes fsync before close so a crash never leaves a\n128|// torn prefix behind.\n129|func writeExclusive(path string, data []byte) error {\n130|\tfile, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREATE|os.O_EXCL, 0o600)\n131|\tif err != nil {\n132|\t\treturn err\n133|\t}\n134|\tif _, err := file.Write(data); err != nil {\n135|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n136|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write exclusive file: %w\", err)\n137|\t}\n138|\tif err := file.Sync(); err != nil {\n139|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n140|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fsync exclusive file: %w\", err)\n141|\t}\n142|\tif err := file.Close(); err != nil {\n143|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"close exclusive file: %w\", err)\n144|\t}\n145|\treturn nil\n146|}\n147|\n148|// syncDirectory fsyncs a directory so an install inside it survives\n149|// a crash. Opening a directory fails on Windows, where the install\n150|// itself is the durability boundary; there the sync is skipped,\n151|// never faked.\n152|func syncDirectory(path string) error {\n153|\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n154|\t\treturn nil\n155|\t}\n156|\tdirectory, err := os.Open(path)\n157|\tif err != nil {\n158|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"open directory for fsync: %w\", err)\n159|\t}\n160|\tdefer func() { _ = directory.Close() }()\n161|\tif err := directory.Sync(); err != nil {\n162|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fsync directory: %w\", err)\n163|\t}\n164|\treturn nil\n165|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":282,"recorded_at":1780531400000559,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcca5057262adb3ab84218faf24","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessckpt captures typed Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 closures over\n2|// provider identity, workspace manifests, the task-board bundle, terminal\n3|// evidence, and the source head (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-14yo67).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections 5.4\n6|// (Checkpoint Record), 10.5-10.6 (Materialization Plan/Journal closure\n7|// inputs), and 13.12-13.13 (failure matrix and crash/restart outcome\n8|// gate). The task scope cites the same section numbers of v0.5.0; the\n9|// headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n10|//\n11|// The package owns capture and durable install only. It reuses the\n12|// landed shared owners and never duplicates them:\n13|//\n14|//   - internal/canonicaljson owns the closed Checkpoint Record shape\n15|//     and the canonical omit-self digest (checkpoint_id).\n16|//   - internal/sessrepo owns record attestation\n17|//     (AttestCheckpointRecord) and the event chain the source head\n18|//     binds against (ListEvents).\n19|//   - internal/sessquery owns semantic admission (admitCheckpoint:\n20|//     owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, event\n21|//     heads at or before the owning lease). Capture pre-checks the\n22|//     variant and head binding it can decide from its inputs so an\n23|//     unpublishable closure is refused before publication, but the\n24|//     admission verdict stays with the consumer; tests drive the\n25|//     consumer on captured records instead of re-implementing it.\n26|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, and timestamp grammar.\n27|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the\n28|//     tests wire to the store hooks.\n29|//\n30|// Refusal taxonomy (SPEC Section 5.4: CP-N1..CP-N4 MUST be rejected\n31|// with incompatible_schema before publication):\n32|//\n33|//   - ErrInvalidCheckpoint wraps canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so\n34|//     errors.Is proves the incompatible_schema class for every\n35|//     unpublishable closure: malformed grammar, closed-shape\n36|//     violations, non-quiescent terminal evidence, missing or\n37|//     doubled persistence members, the wrong persistence variant\n38|//     for the declared session kind, and heads that postdate the\n39|//     owning lease.\n40|//   - Unknown sessions and unknown heads propagate the sessrepo\n41|//     chain-read errors (ErrUnknownSession, ErrUnknownEvent), so\n42|//     errors.Is preserves the owner's vocabulary.\n43|//   - ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the\n44|//     same operation retried with moved inputs, and a digest path\n45|//     holding disagreeing bytes.\n46|//\n47|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp): content-addressed blobs\n48|// installed no-replace (O_EXCL) with fsync before close, operation\n49|// receipts installed no-replace after the blob they name, directory\n50|// fsync after install. A crash leaves either nothing, or complete\n51|// bytes that verify through the canonical owner; an interrupted\n52|// capture is resumed by retrying the same operation with\n53|// byte-identical inputs (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n54|//\n55|// Stated bounds: the raw AdmitRecord path attests shape and the\n56|// variant/head gates it can decide, but chain binding needs the\n57|// caller's repository handle; a nil chain refuses closed rather\n58|// than skipping the gate. Capture does not consult lease records:\n59|// creator-holder binding is decided by the consumer at admission\n60|// (pinned by tests here). Capture performs no provider or\n61|// task-board I/O and offers no CLI surface.\n62|package sessckpt","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
