tyRecord\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateProviderIdentityRecord validates the Section 5.5 provider identity shape; the host-side destination-adapter read and carry of that record is additionally implemented in internal/provhost CheckIdentity (see the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings), and no clause of Section 5.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:5.6\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateWorkspaceGroupRecord\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateWorkspaceGroupRecord validates the Section 5.6 workspace group shape; workspace group membership and union behaviour is not implemented and no clause of Section 5.6 is enumerated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:7.2\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.2; the Section 7.2 host envelope (framing, deadlines, size limits, dispatch, and recovery) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, and no clause of Section 7.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 7 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:7.3\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unmeasured\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.3; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 7.3, because the closed Provider Manifest states its obligations as a required-member table, a 16-entry operation registry and exactly 7 capability names rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure this section - and the closed manifest is implemented in internal/provhost DecodeManifest, exercised by the provhost conformance suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:3.2\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/localstore/paths.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ResolvePaths\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"AC-PATH-001\\\",\\n        \\\"localstore-path-registry\\\",\\n        \\\"localstore-layout-owner-only\\\",\\n        \\\"localstore-digest-path-v1\\\",\\n        \\\"localstore-immutable-blob-install\\\",\\n        \\\"localstore-sqlite-projection\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ResolvePaths implements the owner-only Section 3.2 path registry, but no clause of Section 3.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about its obligations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:3.3\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n     