{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cce7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcc-09d6-79d1-9b97-6e93479b8dc1"},"sequence":1230,"recorded_at":1780531400002455,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"410e85d5-c650-4a55-ae65-44f1be1f0a3d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcf-9bcb-7672-a656-02a86cd4eb1e"},"task_id":"01a0adcf-9bcb-7672-a656-02a86cd4eb1e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcf-9bcb-7672-a656-02a86cd4eb1e","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1623 line(s) above)\n1624|## Session Repository and Append-Only Event Chain\n1625|\n1626|[`internal/sessrepo`](internal/sessrepo) persists and validates Session Records\n1627|and per-session event chains with source sequence continuity (pinned v0.5.0\n1628|Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2, 5.7, 14.4). `Open` binds a repository to the sessions\n1629|namespace beneath a data root. `CreateSession` validates one Session Record\n1630|through `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity` and stores its bytes verbatim;\n1631|`AppendEvent` validates one Session Event the same way and links it onto the\n1632|chain only when the continuity rules hold: the first event links exactly the\n1633|Session Record at sequence 1, within one lease the sequence increases by\n1634|exactly one with no repeat and each event references the prior authoritative\n1635|event, a successor lease restarts at 1, a same-epoch second lease diverges,\n1636|and a lower epoch is stale. Records and events live as content-addressed\n1637|`0600` files installed no-replace through the exclusive create (the blob\n1638|install leads with `O_EXCL` and only compares on an `EEXIST` loss, so the\n1639|no-replace property holds across processes the in-process mutex cannot see);\n1640|the chain index (`chain.json`) is replaced atomically after the blob it\n1641|names, and every load re-verifies each digest and re-folds the index through\n1642|the same append rules, so a torn, tampered, reordered, or substituted store\n1643|fails closed instead of deriving state from it. The load re-verification\n1644|attests stored bindings through `VerifyObjectIdentity` and refuses a blob\n1645|whose self field is not `event_id` or whose digest disagrees with the index\n1646|at its named arms — entry decodes refuse a foreign schema before verifying,\n1647|while the load path recomputes whatever digest stored bytes claim and then\n1648|refuses it.\n1649|\n1650|The chain is append-only in both obligations. Appends succeed in order, and\n1651|no production entry rewrites or deletes: duplicate creates, colliding records\n1652|under one session ID, and repeats at a chained sequence are refused, and\n1653|losing-lease branches are preserved as immutable blobs without ever entering\n1654|the authoritative chain. A byte-identical retry of a chained event returns its\n1655|existing reference, so a retry after a crashed commit is safe; a crashed\n1656|commit counts as committed and a retry names the terminal state.\n1657|`CreateSession` runs four durable steps (session directory, record, events\n1658|directory, chain index) and an interrupted create resumes on retry: a bare\n1659|directory or a record without a chain completes, a completed create names\n1660|the terminal state, and a colliding record or a chain without a record is\n1661|refused. `BeforeWrite` and `AfterCommit` connect the outer write boundaries\n1662|to `secconftest` crash points in tests, and `AfterCreateStep` fires after\n1663|each of the four interior create steps, so every crash window is drivable:\n1664|a fault before the durable write carries `safe_retry` with nothing mutated,\n1665|a fault past any durable step carries `recoverable_parked_state` with the\n1666|parked state resuming on the identical retry. `Resolve` implements the local\n1667|steps of name resolution — exact live name, ASCII case-fold collision refusal\n1668|with `name_ambiguous`, UUID routing over healthy sessions only — and\n1669|`ListSessions` exposes stored identity plus chain-head facts, with a parked\n1670|session returned per session (`Parked` with the `recoverable_parked_state`\n1671|blocking reason and the same-operation retry) instead of failing the whole\n1672|repository: a bare directory retries `CreateSession` with the record for its\n1673|ID, a record without a chain retries the byte-identical record (full-content\n1674|equality, not length-only), and a torn store past the create window has no\n1675|healing retry — the operator removes\n1676|`<data-root>/sessions/<session-id>` after confirming no host will retry, and\n1677|the listing heals. The two content-equality comparisons (resume in\n1678|`sessrepo.go`, blob install in `chain.go`) each ship a same-length differing\n1679|vector and a length-only narrowing mutant.\n1680|\n1681|The package derives no lifecycle state, renders no list/status output, learns\n1682|no peer names, and takes no lease-arbitration decision: the Section 5.7\n1683|reducer, the full Section 2.3 order with interactive choice, Section 14.4\n1684|rendering, and cross-partition lease convergence belong to the sibling leaves\n1685|that build on these entries. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and\n1686|no runtime capability claim.\n1687|\n1688|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n1689|\n1690|```bash\n1691|go test ./internal/sessrepo -count=1\n1692|go test ./internal/sessrepo -cover -count=1\n1693|```\n1694|\n1695|The unfiltered package run derives the 35-site refusal inventory from the\n1696|production source through `internal/invcore` (5 in `sessrepo.go`, 25 in\n1697|`chain.go`, 5 in `store.go`): every `refuse` call site must\n1698|have a boundary-driven negative path (`Open`, `CreateSession`, `AppendEvent`,\n1699|`GetRecord`, `GetEvent`, `ListEvents`, `ListSessions`, `Resolve`), every\n1700|exercised site must derive, sentinel wraps outside the funnel fail, and the\n1701|observed sentinel set must equal the derived roster. The load re-verification\n1702|holds three separate rows — verify failure, non-`event_id` self field, and\n1703|index-disagreeing digest — each with its own boundary-driven plant. The alias\n1704|audit keeps the funnel and the watched owner delegations\n1705|(`VerifyObjectIdentity`, `DecodeStrictObject`, `CheckUUIDv7`,\n1706|`CheckUint53Bounds`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7`, `ParseUUIDv4`) in\n1707|direct-call position, proved by plants that include an import alias and a var\n1708|binding in both directions. A second derived census covers the two\n1709|content-equality comparisons (`bytes.Equal` in `sessrepo.go` resume and\n1710|`chain.go` blob install, plus the `string(...) ==` spelling form): every\n1711|derived site needs a registered same-length vector, an unregistered site, an\n1712|orphan row, or an unclassifiable spelling fails the gate, and the static\n1713|census runs on every full package run whether the suite is green or red, so a\n1714|red test masks no plant. The mutation battery (33 applied, 33 killed, 0\n1715|survivors; 16 narrowing, 10 arm-deletion, 4 census-only, 3 audit-only; plus\n1716|NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls) covers the write, load, and recovery\n1717|paths — including the per-session parked channel and both content-equality\n1718|comparisons — and is recorded on the owning task board item.\n1719|\n1720|## Session State Reducer\n1721|\n1722|[`internal/sessstate`](internal/sessstate) derives deterministic logical-session\n1723|state from the immutable records (pinned v0.5.0 Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2, 5.7,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
